  README.md-12- The repository hosts curated, versioned **GraalVM reachability metadata** for community JVM libraries and frameworks, plus the test harness, CI, and AI automation that keep the metadata correct and up to date.
  README.md-13- 
  README.md:14: Reachability metadata describes reflection, JNI, resource access, serialization, and proxy use that GraalVM `native-image` cannot determine through static analysis. By centralizing this metadata, the repository allows libraries that are not yet self-contained for native compilation to "just work" with `native-image` when consumed via the GraalVM Gradle and Maven plugins.
  README.md-15- 
  README.md-16- ## 2. Users and Use Cases
  README.md-153-     NBT->>NBT: for each application dependency,<br/>pick metadata version via index.json<br/>(tested-versions → default-for → latest)
  README.md-154-     NBT->>NI: pass selected metadata directories
  README.md:155:     NI-->>App: native image with reflection / JNI /<br/>resources / serialization / proxies registered
